# Level 1, and the only thing it does is **press L and R**, which no other movie
# in the corpus does at all.
#
# `$80:D1FF player_state_normal` reads four edge-triggered buttons and the
# fourth is `#$0030` -- L or R together -- which spawns a thread at `$82:D8DB`
# and plays sound `$0D`. Both of its branches were untaken by all 42 movies,
# not because they are hard to reach but because forty-two routes had never
# needed that button. That is backlog rather than dilution, and this is the
# input that clears it.
#
# The two branches are a press and *the same press again too soon*:
#
#   * `$82:D8DB`'s first instruction is `INC $1F98,X`, so the thread sets the
#     player's flag itself.
#   * `$80:D29C` requires that flag to be **clear**. When it is not, the press
#     is eaten and the flag is cleared instead -- so the first press after the
#     thread has run does nothing except re-arm the button.
#
# So `psn_spawn` needs one press and `psn_spawn_swallowed` needs a second one
# while the first is still up. The movie presses L five times at 40-frame
# spacing, then R five times at 12, and the close spacing is what takes the
# swallow.
#
# The prefix through frame 1484 is `movies/level1.zmv`'s title mashing verbatim.
